{{- /*
	caddy.env - production's Caddy container, which serves both stacks:
	  CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN                               prod's /caddy
	  STAGING_BASIC_AUTH_USER, STAGING_BASIC_AUTH_HASH   staging's /caddy
	Both folders are rendered whole, names unchanged.

	The ONE template with two secret calls: a listSecrets call reads a
	single environment. The Agent change-detects a template through the
	ETag of its LAST secret call only, so the order is deliberate:
	  1. staging /caddy - a change here is NOT detected on its own;
	  2. prod /caddy    - a change here re-renders the whole file (both
	                      folders, fresh) and recreates Caddy.
	A forgotten Cloudflare token update would fail silently at the next
	certificate renewal; a forgotten basic-auth update shows at once (the new
	password is refused). After changing staging's basic auth, force a
	re-render: README.md, "caddy.env reads two environments".

	The bcrypt hash holds $ characters: values are single-quoted, or Compose
	would expand them. Ignores the environment slug (always staging + prod);
	rendered for the prod stack only.
*/ -}}
# leviosa caddy.env - rendered from Infisical staging/caddy and prod/caddy
# by the Infisical Agent. Do not edit: change the value in Infisical.
{{- range listSecrets "__LEVIOSA_PROJECT_ID__" "staging" "/caddy" }}
{{ .Key }}='{{ .Value }}'
{{- end }}
{{- range listSecrets "__LEVIOSA_PROJECT_ID__" "prod" "/caddy" }}
{{ .Key }}='{{ .Value }}'
{{- end }}
